  The thing about the Ascension Run, and maybe Nethack in general,
is that the better players tend to die from either instadeaths or
bad situations that snowball into disaster.

  I've watched players on NAO, that seemed totally unprepared, 
breeze through the Ascension run.  Others got slowed down a little
upon entering the Plane of Air, and ended up surrounded by
monsters six deep in the middle of the plane.  No wands of teleport
meant no hope.

  So, imho, the trick is to get to the co-aligned high temple
on Astral as quickly as possible.  The altar then becomes 
your guaranteed escape route if everything goes pear-shaped.

  Far and away the worst thing about the conflict, invisible/
displaced, haste self, zap wand of tele and #jump technique is 
that it's so safe it's boring.  (As long as you get moving
and keep moving.)


